            'liq.ui.structural_wall_thickness_for_pressure_loads': 'Chamber wall thickness, mm. With Regenerative cooling this is the LINER: the hot-gas wall from the gas side to the channel base (the hot wall of the thermal chain and of the liner stress check); the coolant pressure is carried by the closeout (Closeout Thickness). With other cooling types it is the single structural wall that carries the chamber pressure. Server accepted range 0.2-500 mm. Empty: Regenerative - HRMA uses a 1 mm liner and says so; other types - HRMA sizes the wall for the chamber pressure with your safety factor (next standard plate).',
