            'liq.ui.temperature_of_coolant_entering_cooling_system': 'Coolant temperature at the cooling jacket inlet, K. Sets the coolant properties along the channels and its temperature rise budget. Empty: 115 K for methane and 25 K for LH2 (normal boiling point plus pump heating, NIST WebBook), 300 K for the other fuels; the value used is stated. Accepted 20-700 K.',
            'liq.ui.the_liquid_fuel_component_rp_1': 'The liquid fuel component. RP-1: refined kerosene (810 kg/m³), high density, room temperature storable. LH2: cryogenic liquid hydrogen (71 kg/m³), highest specific impulse, complex handling. Methane: storable at moderate pressure (422 kg/m³), Mars missions. MMH/UDMH: hypergolic fuels for spacecraft.',
            'liq.ui.the_liquid_oxidizer_component_lox_cryogenic': 'The liquid oxidizer. LOX: cryogenic liquid oxygen. N2O4: storable nitrogen tetroxide, hypergolic with hydrazine fuels. Selects the propellant pair, so the combustion solution, the propellant densities and the tank sizing.',
            'liq.ui.titanium_6al4v': 'Titanium Ti-6Al-4V',
            'liq.ui.total_impulse': 'Total Impulse',
            'liq.ui.total_number_of_injection_element_pairs': 'Number of injection elements (count). It fixes the hole count of the injector circuits; the hole diameters then follow from the flow areas. Unlike doublet, showerhead, coaxial: holes per circuit (one fuel + one oxidizer hole per element). Like-on-like doublet: same-fluid PAIRS per circuit (two holes each), 1-60 because the circuit planner allows at most 120 holes per circuit; more is rejected, not clamped. Not used for the pintle (a single element; the field is hidden). Accepted band 1-20000. Empty: each circuit plans the fewest holes inside its 0.5-2.5 mm diameter band and the answer says so.',
            'liq.ui.trajectory_analysis': 'Trajectory Analysis',
